[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: ai.strictdoc cannot be published as a devenv facet while options-doc demands exact HM parity

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-STRICTDOC-DEVENV-MODULE-NOT-PUBLISHED
TITLE: ai.strictdoc cannot be published as a devenv facet while options-doc demands exact HM parity
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
packages/strictdoc-grammar/modules/devenv/ is imported by PATH from devenv.nix
rather than exposed as modules.devenv on the package barrel, and that is a
constraint rather than a preference.

flake.nix builds devenvModules.nix-agentic-tools from collectFacet ["modules"
"devenv"], which walks every barrel. checks/options-doc.nix then diffs that
merged devenv option tree against homeManagerModules.default option name for
option name. Any ai.* option with a devenv facet and no home-manager facet
fails that check by construction, and ai.strictdoc has no home-manager half by
ruling (MECH-STRICTDOC-DEVENV-MODULE).

So there are three ways forward and none is free. Add a home-manager facet,
which the ruling declined. Teach options-doc an explicit devenv-only allowlist,
which weakens the parity gate for every future module. Or leave the module
unpublished, which is what happened, at the cost that a consumer of this
repository's flake cannot import ai.strictdoc at all -- only this repository's
own devenv.nix reaches it.

Nothing records the third cost anywhere a consumer would see it.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Noticed while stripping the wrap out of the overlay: the module header asserted
this constraint and cited a node UID that did not exist, so the reasoning was
one edit away from being lost entirely.
<<<
